Z||000009||Formula88||08-16-2001||10:45 PM||||I love those VTEC engines!  If I didn't already have my 99 Grand Am as a daily driver, I'd probably be looking for a 96-98 Civic Si.  (And no, I wouldn't modify it).<P>Just imagine what kind of power we could get out of some American iron with that technology!  I'd love to figure out a way to retro fit it. <P>And how about the iVTEC in the new Acura RSX Type S?  It not only varies the valve lift, but advances and retards the cam depending on driving conditions.  It even gives enough overlap under cruise so that the exhaust gas reversion gets rid of the need for a separate EGR valve!  Ingenious.<P>Oh, and a pretty funny sound clip too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
